diff --git a/docs/docker-deployment.md b/docs/docker-deployment.md
index f6eca78..9fcde89 100644
--- a/docs/docker-deployment.md
+++ b/docs/docker-deployment.md
@@ -101,6 +101,22 @@ Set `BASE_URL` to the full URL where your Fizzy instance is accessible:
 docker run --env BASE_URL=https://fizzy.example.com ...
 ```
 
+#### Push notifications (optional)
+
+Fizzy can send notifications to the phones and desktops of people who turn them on, as well as showing them in the tray.
+This needs a pair of VAPID keys, which you can generate once with:
+
+```sh
+docker run --rm ghcr.io/basecamp/fizzy:main bin/rails runner 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts "VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=#{key.public_key}", "VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=#{key.private_key}"'
+```
+
+Then set both as environment variables, keeping the private key secret:
+
+- `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` - the public key, which browsers use to subscribe
+- `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` - the private key, which Fizzy uses to sign pushes
+
+Push notifications are only offered when both keys are set.
+
 #### S3 storage (optional)
 
 If you'd prefer that uploaded files were stored in an S3 bucket rather than in your mounted volume, you can set that up.
diff --git a/docs/kamal-deployment.md b/docs/kamal-deployment.md
index 5dcd257..de61632 100644
--- a/docs/kamal-deployment.md
+++ b/docs/kamal-deployment.md
@@ -36,6 +36,7 @@ We've added comments to that file to highlight what each setting needs to be, bu
 - `env/clear/BASE_URL`: The public URL of your Fizzy instance (e.g., `https://fizzy.example.com`). Used when generating links.
 - `env/clear/MAILER_FROM_ADDRESS`: This is the email address that Fizzy will send emails from. It should usually be an address from the same domain where you're running Fizzy.
 - `env/clear/SMTP_ADDRESS`: The address of an SMTP server that you can send email through. You can use a 3rd-party service for this, like Sendgrid or Postmark, in which case their documentation will tell you what to use for this.
+- `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY`: Optional. A pair of keys that lets people get notifications on their phones and desktops. Generate them with `bin/rails runner 'key = WebPush.generate_key; puts key.public_key, key.private_key'`. Put `VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` under `env/clear` and `VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY` under `env/secret` in `config/deploy.yml`, and add the private key to `.kamal/secrets`. Push notifications are only offered when both are set.
 - `env/clear/MULTI_TENANT`: Set to `true` if you want to allow multiple accounts to sign up on your server (by default, Fizzy will allow you to create a single account).
 
 Fizzy also requires a few environment variables to be set up, some of which contain secrets.
